Hint: Recall the perpendicular axis theorem.

Step 1: Find the moment of inertia of each case.The moment of inertia of a thin
circular ring about its diameter is given by;
\(I_1 = \frac{I_z}{2}= \frac{MR^2}{2}~~~~~~[I_z = MR^2]\)
The moment of circular disc about an axis perpendicular to the disc and going
through the centre is given by;
\(I_2 = \frac{MR^2}{2}\)
The moment of inertia of solid cylinder about its axis is given by;
\(I_3 =I_z= \frac{1}{2}MR^2\)
The moment of inertia of solid sphere about its diameter is given by;
\(I_4 =\frac{I_z}{2}= \frac{\frac{2}{5}MR^2}{2}= \frac{MR^2}{5}\)

Step 2:Compare the moment of inertia of different cases.
By comparing the order of different moment inertia we get;
\(I_1=I_2=I_3>I_4\)
